# --- SECRETS: never commit these ---------------------------------------
# Your ESPN session cookies live here. Anyone with them can act as you on
# ESPN. This entry is the only thing keeping them off GitHub.
config/secrets.json
config/secrets.*.json
# ...but the placeholder template must ship, or a fresh clone has no
# instructions for setting credentials up.
!config/secrets.example.json
*.secret.json
.env
.env.*

# --- Regenerable data --------------------------------------------------
# Raw API cache: large, regenerable with `npm run fetch`, and contains more
# of your league than needs publishing. The site reads docs/data/.
data/raw/

# Synthetic test data: `npm run fixtures` regenerates it byte-identically
# from a fixed seed, so there is no reason to carry it in the repo.
data/fixtures/

# NOTE: docs/data/ IS committed on purpose — it is what GitHub Pages serves.
# ...except the money ledger. It is still generated locally, so `npm run serve`
# shows you the full ledger on your machine, but it never reaches the public
# site. Flip site.showMoney in config/league.json and delete this line if you
# later decide to publish it.
docs/data/money.json

# --- Node --------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
